  "name": "Create Asana projects and Google Drive folders from new HubSpot deals",
  "tags": [],
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "cf39de32-9d82-4d80-b7bc-b14727859b3b",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        -80
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 512,
        "height": 1392,
        "content": "# Create Asana projects and Google Drive folders from new HubSpot deals\n\nWho's it for: sales and delivery teams that want every new HubSpot deal to get its own Asana project and Google Drive folder automatically, with the links written back onto the deal.\n\n### How it works\n1. A HubSpot deal-creation webhook fires and its signature is verified.\n2. The deal, its owner, and its associated company are loaded.\n3. If the company has no Drive folder yet, one is created, then a folder for this deal inside it.\n4. An Asana project is created from your project template, named \"Client_[company]. Project_[deal]\".\n5. The folder and project links are saved back onto the HubSpot deal (and the folder onto the company).\n6. The deal owner is emailed both links. A deal created with no company gets a short \"not created\" notice instead.\n\n### Setup\n1. Fill in the Set configuration node: HubSpot app client secret, shared drive ID, parent folder ID for company folders, and your Asana project template GID.\n2. Connect your HubSpot, Google Drive, Asana and Gmail accounts.\n3. Create the custom HubSpot properties this workflow reads and writes (see the template description).\n4. Add this workflow's production webhook URL to a HubSpot deal-creation subscription, then activate the workflow.\n\n### Customization\nChange the project naming pattern in the two \"Create Asana project\" nodes, edit the email wording, or add more HubSpot properties to write back."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
